WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:01.030 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  benigno aquino iii came from a long line  of filipino politicians  he was the son of a much-loved president  as well as a national hero  his father benigno nina aquina jr a  well-known opponent of president  ferdinand marcus  was assassinated at manila airport in  1983.  his killing on the tarmac was described  as brazen  outrageous and shocking  his widow corazon aquino who had stayed  out of politics  took over his role she became the face  of a people power movement  that led to the end of the 21-year rule  by marcus regarded by many as a dictator  she eventually became the first female  president of the philippines  in 1986. his mother's passing in 2009  followed a huge outpouring of grief for  her  a symbol of democracy to many filipinos  she was a catalyst for him to run for  the highest post  in government he was sworn in as the  15th  president in 2010. my parents  sought nothing less and died for nothing  less than democracy  peace and prosperity i am blessed by  this legacy  i shall carry the torch forward at the  end of the day  for a man who had lived for so many  years in his parents shadow  aquino soon came into his own he focused  on fighting corruption  removing a sitting supreme court chief  justice  accused of corruption and jailing his  predecessor  former president gloria macapagal arroyo  for government irregularities  he pushed through a law on reproductive  rights  a feat many warned will be near  impossible  in a nation predominantly roman catholic  during his administration the economy  grew by an average  of more than 6 percent a year he  challenged china's territorial claims in  the south china sea  filing a case to the international  criminal court at the hague  and winning the major ruling declared  most of china's claim  invalid the victory was seen as  unprecedented  but aquino's presidency wasn't without  controversy  the philippines was battered by severe  natural disasters in 2013.  but he was mostly impatient with  criticism  especially with his government's low  response in dealing with typhoon haiyan  one of the strongest storms on record  two years later a botched operation to  capture a fugitive muslim fighter  killed more than 60 people including 44  police officers  and five civilians turning the armed  encounter  into aquino's biggest political crisis  he leaves behind a mixed legacy  but said all he ever wanted was to be  remembered  as someone who was given the honor to  serve the people  and he gave his best

